---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '@components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site, legal } from '@config/site';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Evidence Axis handles information from website inquiries, invitation-only intelligence delivery pages, email and business correspondence."
  path="/privacy/"
  noindex={false}
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy" meta={[`Last updated ${legal.lastUpdated}`]} />

  <section class="section container">
    <div class="legal measure">
      <p class="legal__intro">
        This note explains what information {site.name} receives through this website, invitation-only
        intelligence deliveries and business correspondence, and how that information is used. Any paid
        engagement is also governed by the terms agreed for that specific project.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is operated publicly by {legal.publicOperator}, whose legal name is
        {' '}{legal.operatorLegalName}. Privacy questions can be sent to
        {' '}<a href="mailto:hello@evidenceaxis.com">hello@evidenceaxis.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If an engagement is contracted through {legal.internationalInvoicingEntity}, that company
        may also receive the client and transaction details needed to contract, invoice, keep
        business records and deliver the work. The applicable contracting party is identified in
        writing before paid work begins.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you provide</h2>
      <p>
        If you use the website inquiry form or contact us by email, we receive the details you choose
        to send. These may include your name, work email, company, company website, role, competitive
        decision or research question, named competitors and related context. We use this information
        to understand the inquiry, assess fit, respond and, where agreed, prepare the relevant work.
      </p>

      <h2>Invitation-only intelligence deliveries</h2>
      <p>
        Evidence Axis may prepare a company-specific Competitive Intelligence Gift without a prior
        request when a relevant public competitive trigger is visible. The work is built from lawful,
        publicly accessible information. The private delivery link may identify the intended company
        so the correct package can be delivered and operational engagement can be measured.
      </p>

      <h2>Intelligence-delivery tracking</h2>
      <p>
        A company-specific intelligence delivery page may record limited operational events so we can
        confirm whether the work was successfully received and used. For the current delivery system,
        these events can include the delivery page being viewed, the Executive Intelligence Deck being
        opened, the Evidence Appendix being opened, or the recipient clicking the decision-conversation
        route. The event payload sent to our business inbox identifies the company, the unique delivery
        slug, the event type and the event timestamp. This is delivery confirmation and product-learning
        data, not advertising tracking.
      </p>
      <p>
        The current first-sprint implementation uses session storage only to avoid sending the same
        operational event repeatedly during one browser session. It does not use an advertising cookie
        or build an advertising profile.
      </p>

      <h2>Business correspondence</h2>
      <p>
        If we correspond about a possible or active engagement, we keep the information reasonably
        needed to carry out and account for that work. We do not sell it, and we do not use it for
        advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Technical information</h2>
      <p>
        Basic technical information, such as standard server request data, may be processed to keep
        the site available and secure. The current site does not use advertising trackers or advertising
        cookies. Website inquiry submissions and the operational delivery events described above are
        transmitted through FormSubmit for delivery to our business inbox. If additional analytics or
        cookies are introduced, this notice will be updated and consent will be requested where required.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Service providers may process limited information where needed for website hosting, email,
        form delivery, file storage, invoicing or delivery. They are given only the information needed
        for that function and remain subject to their own security, privacy and legal obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep inquiry, delivery and engagement information for as long as reasonably necessary for
        the purpose it was provided or collected, and for legitimate business and record-keeping needs,
        then remove it. If you would like relevant information removed, email
        {' '}<a href="mailto:hello@evidenceaxis.com">hello@evidenceaxis.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what inquiry or delivery information we hold about you and request that it be
        corrected or removed. Depending on your location, additional rights may apply; we will honor
        applicable requirements. Requests can be sent to the email address below.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or privacy requests can be sent to
        {' '}<a href="mailto:hello@evidenceaxis.com">hello@evidenceaxis.com</a>. Postal correspondence
        concerning an engagement should be sent to the contracting address stated in that
        engagement's written terms or invoice.
      </p>

      <p class="legal__foot mono">Last updated {legal.lastUpdated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal__intro { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--text); }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--space-xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
    padding-top: var(--space-s); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .legal p { color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-s); }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); }
  .legal__foot { margin-top: var(--space-xl); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-faint); }
</style>